# Generated datasets -- reproducible from common/make_dataset.py (144 MB).
data/
_archive/

# Private working notes. The root report is the shareable detailed companion to
# the README and is intentionally versioned.

# Local AI-assistant instructions and session state.
CLAUDE.md
.codex/
.agents/
AGENTS.md

# vipe_slow is a VENDORED NVIDIA ViPE checkout (its upstream .git was removed so
# this repo owns it directly, not as a submodule). Keep the source + launchers +
# the 31 MB test_video/ clips (the ViPE reproduce command globs all of them), but
# exclude the heavy things a reader does not need:
#   test_{4,8}gpus/  ~1.5 GB of raw depth/rgb/mask output -- the original 4-vs-8
#                    evidence, now superseded by the committed results/vipe_prodcached/
#                    JSON, so the finding reproduces without shipping the GB.
#   *.so             the compiled vipe_ext extension -- rebuilt by `pip install -e .`
vipe_slow/test_4gpus/
vipe_slow/test_8gpus/
vipe_slow/**/*.so

# Orphaned legacy scripts, not part of the reproducible pipeline (nothing in the
# harness or docs calls them) and they hardcode absolute scratch paths belonging to
# other researchers (HF cache, cookies, dataset CSVs). Kept on disk, out of git.
vipe_slow/run.sh
vipe_slow/scripts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts: EXCLUDE the bulk (555 MB), COMMIT the evidence (~1.1 MB).
#
# results/ is almost entirely ViPE depth/rgb/mask outputs that nobody reading
# this repo needs. But the summaries ARE the evidence: every number in README.md
# is derived from them, and a reader who cannot open them has to take the tables
# on faith. So the JSON summaries, per-worker shards, load traces and
# launcher logs are committed -- 226 files, ~1.1 MB.
#
# Four gitignore behaviours make this fiddly. Each one cost an iteration, and the
# result was verified with `git check-ignore` over all 374 real files rather than
# by eyeballing the patterns:
#   1. git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a bare `results/` makes
#      every later negation unreachable. Exclude files (`*`), keep dirs (`!*/`).
#   2. Depth is literal: `results/*/*` does not match `results/a/b/c`. Every
#      depth needs its own exclude line.
#   3. LAST matching pattern wins, so ALL negations must come after ALL of the
#      broad excludes. Interleaving them per-depth silently loses.
#   4. There are NO trailing comments. `!results/*/sweep.json  # note` makes the
#      comment part of the pattern, so the rule matches nothing -- silently.
#      Every comment here is on its own line for that reason.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Exclude files at each depth, but keep the directories walkable (1, 2).
results/*
!results/*/
results/*/*
!results/*/*/
results/*/*/*
!results/*/*/*/
results/*/*/*/*

# Re-include the evidence: after every exclude above (3), no trailing comments (4).
#   sweep.json         the sweep driver's row-by-row record
#   summary.json       movebench: merged scores + timing + shard imbalance
#   vipe_summary.json  vipe: same
#   ray_run.json       ray: cold start, threads/actor, detected CPUs
#   shard_*.json       per-worker: per-sample cpu_s / gpu_busy_s
#   loadavg.txt        the 1 Hz load trace -- how thread-storms are caught
#   *.log              launcher stdout, incl. the THREAD MISMATCH check
!results/*/sweep.json
!results/*/*/summary.json
!results/*/*/vipe_summary.json
!results/*/*/ray_run.json
!results/*/*/shard_*.json
!results/*/*/loadavg.txt
!results/*/logs/*.log
!results/*/*/logs/*.log

# The two load-balancing runs (movebench_jit{fork,ray}_g8) were written one level
# shallower -- directly under results/<run>/ with no per-cell dir -- so they need
# their own depth-2 negations. These hold the 1.318x -> 1.15x imbalance evidence.
!results/*/summary.json
!results/*/ray_run.json
!results/*/shard_*.json
!results/*/loadavg.txt

# The heavy ViPE outputs (depth zips, rgb, masks, pickles). Last word, so it
# beats the shard_*.json / *.log negations above.
results/*/*/artifacts/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.so

# hydra's default run dir
outputs/
.hydra/

# NOTE: this repo is deliberately figure-free -- every result is a table read from
# committed results/*.json. There is no figures/ directory and no plotting script.
